{Possible Drops: Low Grade Medical Supplies, Beautiful Flower, Innovative Technical Manual}

Faleris is a Fire element Pal. When it finds its prey it unleashes a whirlwind of flames, burning the entire area to ash. Faleris breath is known for its pleasing scent. Faleris is a large avian Pal serving as a reference to a falcon. The majority of its body is colored ebony black, while the middle parts are scarlet red. The edge of its wings and claws of its feet are colored old gold. The feathers atop its head resemble the plumes of Roman helmets. This Pal can be aggressive towards the player.

{Partner Skill: Scorching Predator - Can be ridden as a flying mount. While fighting together, Ice Pals drop more items when defeated. (Requires Faleris Saddle)}

{Work Suitability: Kindling 3, Transporting 3}

{Possible Drops: Flame Organ}

Orserk is a Dragon/Electric element Pal. It sends electricity into its foes' wounds, roasting them from the inside out. Fights between Orserk end in the blink of an eye. Orserk is a bipedal dragon with black scales marked with yellow zig-zags, a pair of yellowish scythe-like eyebrows, a pair of yellow clawed boots and a pair of electricity wings. This Pal is usually aggressive towards the player.

{Partner Skill: Ferocious Thunder Dragon - While fighting together, Water Pals drop more items when defeated.}

{Work Suitability: Generating Electricity 4, Handiwork 2, Transporting 3}

{Possible Drops: Electric Organ}

Shadowbeak is a Dark element Pal. Born from the depths of insanity, its very existence should not be. Having lost all genetic ties to other Pals, one wonders if it could still even be considered a Pal. Shadowbeak is a griffin covered in gray fur and feathers, and black bird-like feet equipped with claws. A black and neon blue ring with spear-tipped edges circles its mid-torso. This Pal can only be encountered in the wild inside the No. 3 Wildlife Sanctuary roaming and sometimes grazing.

{Partner Skill: Modified DNA - Can be ridden as a flying mount. Enhances Dark attacks while mounted. (Requires Shadowbeak Saddle)}

{Work Suitability: Gathering 1}

{Possible Drops: Pal Metal Ingot, Carbon Fiber, Innovative Technical Manual}

Paladius is a Neutral element Pal. In the past, he and Necromus were a single species. They say that they are an existence that has freed themselves from all negative feelings, but the depths of their eyes harbor traces of resentment. Paladius is a centaur with light blue armor trimmed with golden markings, a pair of wings on his helmet and is armed with a shield and lance for combat. Attacks in tandem with Necromus and is hostile towards the player. As a Legendary Pal, it comes with the Legend passive skill. 

{Partner Skill: Holy Winged Knight - You can ride on its back to move around. While riding, you can triple jump. (Requires Paladius Saddle)}

{Work Suitability: Mining 2, Lumbering 2}

{Possible Drops: Pal Metal Ingot, Diamond}

Necromus is a Dark element Pal. Once he and Paladius were a single species. They say it is the manifestation of negative feelings, but the depths of their eyes contain traces of compassion. Necromus is a centaur with black armor etched in red markings, a single red wing on his helmet and is armed with a pair of red lances for combat. It attacks in tandem with Paladius is hostile towards player. Note that Necromus is nocturnal, but Paladius is not. As a Legendary Pal, it comes with the Legend passive skill.

{Partner Skill: Black Knight of the Abyss - You can ride on its back to move around. While riding, you can double jump. (Requires Necromus Saddle)}

{Work Suitability: Mining 2, Lumbering 2}

{Possible Drops: Pal Metal Ingot, Large Pal Soul}

Frostallion is an Ice Element Pal. Guardian deity of Palpagos Island, known as the Winter Caller. In the past, when a calamity struck the land, it soared into the sky and sealed away the threat by casting the island into an eternal winter. Frostallion is a Pegasus with white fur and wings, its mane and tails are grey. Its adorned with chunks of ice on its hooves, legs and forehead. Frostallion is usually passive until attacked. Once engaged in combat Frostallion is hyper aggressive in it's attacks, chaining multiple attacks in rapid succession. Unless properly prepared, players at max level may find defeating the Frostalion Alpha a challenge.As a Legendary Pal, it comes with the Legend passive skill.

{Partner Skill: Ice Steed - Can be ridden as a flying mount. Changes the player's attack type to ice and enhances Ice attacks while mounted. (Requires Frostallion Saddle)}

{Work Suitability: Cooling 4}

{Possible Drops: Ice Organ, Diamond}

Jetragon is a Dragon element Pal. Looks over the island of Palpagos from the ends of the sky. When the calamity awakens again, splitting the earth and setting the heavens on fire, he will destroy it with a glare of complete obliteration. Jetragon is a flying jet-like draconic pal. It is a dull blue and has an off-white stomach and lower jaw. The top of its head features what resembles a black helmet with protruding horns that have bright red-orange stripes. It has bulky darker blue hands that sport two claws, the wrists of Jetragon have an orange stripe. The thighs of Jetragon feature hollowed out parts that resemble jet engines. The feet on Jetragon look similar to its hands but lack stripes. Jetragon's tail is long and greatly resembles the tail of an airplane, its tail is a darker blue and has off-white stripes present. Its back features what resembles a black seat and has four orange spikes. For each of these spikes, it features large bright magenta wings present. It tend to be aggressive towards the player upon sight, attacking unprovoked.
As a Legendary Pal, it comes with the Legend passive skill.

{Partner Skill: Aerial missile - You can ride on its back to fly. While riding, you can continuously fire with a rocket launcher. (Requires Jetragon's Missile Launcher)}

{Work Suitability: Gathering 3}

{Possible Drops: Pure Quartz, Polymer, Carbon Fiber, Diamond}

Bellanoir is a Dark elemental Pal. It is also a Raid-exclusive Pal. Without existing, she quietly gazed upon the world. One day, she was seized with a longing to be seen. With unbridled lust for vengeance against reality, thus was born the Eclipsed Siren. Bellanoir is a tall, witch-like humanoid with a black gown-like body. Around its waist, there are red, eye-like patterns. Instead of legs, blueish-purple flames flicker beneath its skirt. Its arms have frayed sleeves ending in three white triangles, resembling hands. The left eye has long eyelashes and a red pupil, while blue hair covers the right eye. An antler-like protrusion extends from the left side of its forehead, starting blue and fading to light purple at the tip. Behavior, and moves are currently unknown.

{Partner Skill: Nightmare Iris - When activated, attacks targeted enemy with a powerful Nightmare Ray.}

{Work Suitability: Handiwork 2, Medicine Production 4, Transporting 2}

{Possible Drops: Currently Under Investigation, Ancient Civilization Core, Multiclimate undershirt +1, Huge Dark Egg (Containing Bellanoir), Training Crystal, Training Manual (XL)}

Selyne is a Dark/Neutral elemental Pal. The object floating behind, resembling the moon, is said to gradually become more circular with each passing generation. No one knows what will happen when the moon is full. Selyne is a humanoid pal wearing a black and gray dress with golden jewelry. It wears a golden crescent on her forehead and has a colorful crescent-like gem for it to sit on. Selyne is aggressive towards the player and will attack on sight.

{Partner Skill: Celestial Darkness - Can be ridden as a flying mount.
Enhances Neutral and Dark attacks while mounted.}

{Work Suitability: Handiwork 4, Medicine Production 3, Transporting 3}

